From: NixOS surface-laptop-ultra packaging <root@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] hid-multitouch: bind ELAN 04F3:3358 to MT_CLS_WIN_8

Surface Laptop Ultra touchpad (MSHW0734, ELAN 04F3:3358, I2C HID): a
Windows Precision Touchpad with a per-contact Confidence bit, but its
PTPHQA feature blob (usage 0xff0000c5) is 4 bytes instead of 256, so
hid-core groups it as generic multitouch and hid-multitouch never maps
Confidence -> MT_TOOL_PALM (no palm rejection). Add the device-table
entry binding 04F3:3358 to MT_CLS_WIN_8.

HAND-WRITTEN: hunk positions are for linux 7.x hid-multitouch.c; verify
against the target tree and adjust the I2C_HID_QUIRK / HID_ANY_ID
context lines as needed before building.

--- a/drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c
@@ -2103,6 +2103,11 @@ static const struct hid_device_id mt_devices[] = {
 			HID_USB_DEVICE(USB_VENDOR_ID_CIRQUE,
 					USB_DEVICE_ID_CIRQUE_1215) },
 
+	/* Microsoft Surface Laptop Ultra touchpad (MSHW0734) */
+	{ .driver_data = MT_CLS_WIN_8,
+	  HID_DEVICE(BUS_I2C, HID_GROUP_MULTITOUCH_WIN_8, 0x04f3, 0x3358) },
+
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(hid, mt_devices);
